{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pagination state is stored on the table using the following shape:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type PaginationState = {\n  pageIndex: number\n  pageSize: number\n}\n\nexport type PaginationTableState = {\n  pagination: PaginationState\n}\n\nexport type PaginationInitialTableState = {\n  pagination?: Partial<PaginationState>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"manualpagination","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manualPagination"}]},{"type":"code","value":"manualPagination?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables manual pagination. If this option is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the table will not automatically paginate rows using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPaginationRowModel()"},{"type":"text","value":" and instead will expect you to manually paginate the rows before passing them to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side pagination and aggregation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"pagecount","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageCount"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pageCount?: number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageCount"},{"type":"text","value":" value to the table if you know it. If you do not know how many pages there are, you can set this to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"},{"type":"text","value":". Alternatively, you can provide a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowCount"},{"type":"text","value":" value and the table will calculate the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageCount"},{"type":"text","value":" internally."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rowcount","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowCount"}]},{"type":"code","value":"rowCount?: number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowCount"},{"type":"text","value":" value to the table if you know it. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageCount"},{"type":"text","value":" will be calculated internally from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowCount"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageSize"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"autoresetpageindex","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"autoResetPageIndex"}]},{"type":"code","value":"autoResetPageIndex?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", pagination will be reset to the first page when page-altering state changes eg. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" is updated, filters change, grouping changes, etc."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🧠 Note: This option defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" if "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manualPagination"},{"type":"text","value":" is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onpaginationchange","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onPaginationChange"}]},{"type":"code","value":"onPaginationChange?: OnChangeFn<PaginationState>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If this function is provided, it will be called when the pagination state changes and you will be expected to manage the state yourself. You can pass the managed state back to the table via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions.state.pagination"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getpaginationrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPaginationRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getPaginationRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model after pagination has taken place, but no further."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pagination columns are automatically reordered by default to the start of the columns list. If you would rather remove them or leave them as-is, set the appropriate mode here."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setpagination","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setPagination"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setPagination: (updater: Updater<PaginationState>) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sets or updates the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.pagination"},{"type":"text","value":" state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetpagination","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetPagination"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetPagination: (defaultState?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pagination"}]},{"type":"text","value":" state to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState.pagination"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" can be passed to force a default blank state reset to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[]"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setpageindex","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setPageIndex"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setPageIndex: (updater: Updater<number>) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Updates the page index using the provided function or value."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetpageindex","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetPageIndex"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetPageIndex: (defaultState?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets the page index to its initial state. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultState"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the page index will be reset to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" regardless of initial state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setpagesize","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setPageSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setPageSize: (updater: Updater<number>) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Updates the page size using the provided function or value."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetpagesize","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetPageSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetPageSize: (defaultState?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets the page size to its initial state. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultState"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the page size will be reset to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"10"},{"type":"text","value":" regardless of initial state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getpageoptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPageOptions"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getPageOptions: () => number[]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns an array of page options (zero-index-based) for the current page size."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcanpreviouspage","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCanPreviousPage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCanPreviousPage: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether the table can go to the previous page."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcannextpage","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCanNextPage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCanNextPage: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether the table can go to the next page."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"previouspage","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previousPage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"previousPage: () => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decrements the page index by one, if possible."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"nextpage","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nextPage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"nextPage: () => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Increments the page index by one, if possible."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"firstpage","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"firstPage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"firstPage: () => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sets the page index to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"lastpage","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastPage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"lastPage: () => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sets the page index to the last available page."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getpagecount","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPageCount"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getPageCount: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the page count. If manually paginating or controlling the pagination state, this will come directly from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.pageCount"},{"type":"text","value":" table option, otherwise it will be calculated from the table data using the total row count and current page size."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getprepaginationrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPrePaginationRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getPrePaginationRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model for the table before any pagination has been applied."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getpaginationrowmodel-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPaginationRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getPaginationRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model for the table after pagination has been applied."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"state","text":"State","level":2},{"id":"table-options","text":"Table Options","level":2},{"id":"manualpagination","text":"manualPagination","level":3},{"id":"pagecount","text":"pageCount","level":3},{"id":"rowcount","text":"rowCount","level":3},{"id":"autoresetpageindex","text":"autoResetPageIndex","level":3},{"id":"onpaginationchange","text":"onPaginationChange","level":3},{"id":"getpaginationrowmodel","text":"getPaginationRowModel","level":3},{"id":"table-api","text":"Table API","level":2},{"id":"setpagination","text":"setPagination","level":3},{"id":"resetpagination","text":"resetPagination","level":3},{"id":"setpageindex","text":"setPageIndex","level":3},{"id":"resetpageindex","text":"resetPageIndex","level":3},{"id":"setpagesize","text":"setPageSize","level":3},{"id":"resetpagesize","text":"resetPageSize","level":3},{"id":"getpageoptions","text":"getPageOptions","level":3},{"id":"getcanpreviouspage","text":"getCanPreviousPage","level":3},{"id":"getcannextpage","text":"getCanNextPage","level":3},{"id":"previouspage","text":"previousPage","level":3},{"id":"nextpage","text":"nextPage","level":3},{"id":"firstpage","text":"firstPage","level":3},{"id":"lastpage","text":"lastPage","level":3},{"id":"getpagecount","text":"getPageCount","level":3},{"id":"getprepaginationrowmodel","text":"getPrePaginationRowModel","level":3},{"id":"getpaginationrowmodel-2","text":"getPaginationRowModel","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## State\n\nPagination state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type PaginationState = {\n  pageIndex: number\n  pageSize: number\n}\n\nexport type PaginationTableState = {\n  pagination: PaginationState\n}\n\nexport type PaginationInitialTableState = {\n  pagination?: Partial<PaginationState>\n}\n```\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `manualPagination`\n\n```tsx\nmanualPagination?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables manual pagination. If this option is set to `true`, the table will not automatically paginate rows using `getPaginationRowModel()` and instead will expect you to manually paginate the rows before passing them to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side pagination and aggregation.\n\n### `pageCount`\n\n```tsx\npageCount?: number\n```\n\nWhen manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total `pageCount` value to the table if you know it. If you do not know how many pages there are, you can set this to `-1`. Alternatively, you can provide a `rowCount` value and the table will calculate the `pageCount` internally.\n\n### `rowCount`\n\n```tsx\nrowCount?: number\n```\n\nWhen manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total `rowCount` value to the table if you know it. `pageCount` will be calculated internally from `rowCount` and `pageSize`.\n\n### `autoResetPageIndex`\n\n```tsx\nautoResetPageIndex?: boolean\n```\n\nIf set to `true`, pagination will be reset to the first page when page-altering state changes eg. `data` is updated, filters change, grouping changes, etc.\n\n> 🧠 Note: This option defaults to `false` if `manualPagination` is set to `true`\n\n### `onPaginationChange`\n\n```tsx\nonPaginationChange?: OnChangeFn<PaginationState>\n```\n\nIf this function is provided, it will be called when the pagination state changes and you will be expected to manage the state yourself. You can pass the managed state back to the table via the `tableOptions.state.pagination` option.\n\n### `getPaginationRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPaginationRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model after pagination has taken place, but no further.\n\nPagination columns are automatically reordered by default to the start of the columns list. If you would rather remove them or leave them as-is, set the appropriate mode here.\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setPagination`\n\n```tsx\nsetPagination: (updater: Updater<PaginationState>) => void\n```\n\nSets or updates the `state.pagination` state.\n\n### `resetPagination`\n\n```tsx\nresetPagination: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the **pagination** state to `initialState.pagination`, or `true` can be passed to force a default blank state reset to `[]`.\n\n### `setPageIndex`\n\n```tsx\nsetPageIndex: (updater: Updater<number>) => void\n```\n\nUpdates the page index using the provided function or value.\n\n### `resetPageIndex`\n\n```tsx\nresetPageIndex: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the page index to its initial state. If `defaultState` is `true`, the page index will be reset to `0` regardless of initial state.\n\n### `setPageSize`\n\n```tsx\nsetPageSize: (updater: Updater<number>) => void\n```\n\nUpdates the page size using the provided function or value.\n\n### `resetPageSize`\n\n```tsx\nresetPageSize: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the page size to its initial state. If `defaultState` is `true`, the page size will be reset to `10` regardless of initial state.\n\n### `getPageOptions`\n\n```tsx\ngetPageOptions: () => number[]\n```\n\nReturns an array of page options (zero-index-based) for the current page size.\n\n### `getCanPreviousPage`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanPreviousPage: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether the table can go to the previous page.\n\n### `getCanNextPage`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanNextPage: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether the table can go to the next page.\n\n### `previousPage`\n\n```tsx\npreviousPage: () => void\n```\n\nDecrements the page index by one, if possible.\n\n### `nextPage`\n\n```tsx\nnextPage: () => void\n```\n\nIncrements the page index by one, if possible.\n\n### `firstPage`\n\n```tsx\nfirstPage: () => void\n```\n\nSets the page index to `0`.\n\n### `lastPage`\n\n```tsx\nlastPage: () => void\n```\n\nSets the page index to the last available page.\n\n### `getPageCount`\n\n```tsx\ngetPageCount: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the page count. If manually paginating or controlling the pagination state, this will come directly from the `options.pageCount` table option, otherwise it will be calculated from the table data using the total row count and current page size.\n\n### `getPrePaginationRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPrePaginationRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table before any pagination has been applied.\n\n### `getPaginationRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPaginationRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table after pagination has been applied.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Pagination APIs\nid: pagination\n---\n\n## State\n\nPagination state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type PaginationState = {\n  pageIndex: number\n  pageSize: number\n}\n\nexport type PaginationTableState = {\n  pagination: PaginationState\n}\n\nexport type PaginationInitialTableState = {\n  pagination?: Partial<PaginationState>\n}\n```\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `manualPagination`\n\n```tsx\nmanualPagination?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables manual pagination. If this option is set to `true`, the table will not automatically paginate rows using `getPaginationRowModel()` and instead will expect you to manually paginate the rows before passing them to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side pagination and aggregation.\n\n### `pageCount`\n\n```tsx\npageCount?: number\n```\n\nWhen manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total `pageCount` value to the table if you know it. If you do not know how many pages there are, you can set this to `-1`. Alternatively, you can provide a `rowCount` value and the table will calculate the `pageCount` internally.\n\n### `rowCount`\n\n```tsx\nrowCount?: number\n```\n\nWhen manually controlling pagination, you can supply a total `rowCount` value to the table if you know it. `pageCount` will be calculated internally from `rowCount` and `pageSize`.\n\n### `autoResetPageIndex`\n\n```tsx\nautoResetPageIndex?: boolean\n```\n\nIf set to `true`, pagination will be reset to the first page when page-altering state changes eg. `data` is updated, filters change, grouping changes, etc.\n\n> 🧠 Note: This option defaults to `false` if `manualPagination` is set to `true`\n\n### `onPaginationChange`\n\n```tsx\nonPaginationChange?: OnChangeFn<PaginationState>\n```\n\nIf this function is provided, it will be called when the pagination state changes and you will be expected to manage the state yourself. You can pass the managed state back to the table via the `tableOptions.state.pagination` option.\n\n### `getPaginationRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPaginationRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model after pagination has taken place, but no further.\n\nPagination columns are automatically reordered by default to the start of the columns list. If you would rather remove them or leave them as-is, set the appropriate mode here.\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setPagination`\n\n```tsx\nsetPagination: (updater: Updater<PaginationState>) => void\n```\n\nSets or updates the `state.pagination` state.\n\n### `resetPagination`\n\n```tsx\nresetPagination: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the **pagination** state to `initialState.pagination`, or `true` can be passed to force a default blank state reset to `[]`.\n\n### `setPageIndex`\n\n```tsx\nsetPageIndex: (updater: Updater<number>) => void\n```\n\nUpdates the page index using the provided function or value.\n\n### `resetPageIndex`\n\n```tsx\nresetPageIndex: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the page index to its initial state. If `defaultState` is `true`, the page index will be reset to `0` regardless of initial state.\n\n### `setPageSize`\n\n```tsx\nsetPageSize: (updater: Updater<number>) => void\n```\n\nUpdates the page size using the provided function or value.\n\n### `resetPageSize`\n\n```tsx\nresetPageSize: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the page size to its initial state. If `defaultState` is `true`, the page size will be reset to `10` regardless of initial state.\n\n### `getPageOptions`\n\n```tsx\ngetPageOptions: () => number[]\n```\n\nReturns an array of page options (zero-index-based) for the current page size.\n\n### `getCanPreviousPage`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanPreviousPage: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether the table can go to the previous page.\n\n### `getCanNextPage`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanNextPage: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether the table can go to the next page.\n\n### `previousPage`\n\n```tsx\npreviousPage: () => void\n```\n\nDecrements the page index by one, if possible.\n\n### `nextPage`\n\n```tsx\nnextPage: () => void\n```\n\nIncrements the page index by one, if possible.\n\n### `firstPage`\n\n```tsx\nfirstPage: () => void\n```\n\nSets the page index to `0`.\n\n### `lastPage`\n\n```tsx\nlastPage: () => void\n```\n\nSets the page index to the last available page.\n\n### `getPageCount`\n\n```tsx\ngetPageCount: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the page count. If manually paginating or controlling the pagination state, this will come directly from the `options.pageCount` table option, otherwise it will be calculated from the table data using the total row count and current page size.\n\n### `getPrePaginationRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPrePaginationRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table before any pagination has been applied.\n\n### `getPaginationRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPaginationRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table after pagination has been applied.\n"}
